themselves, as distinct from the copyrighted source they modify), `tools/`
(excluding the vendored compat libraries, see below), and the READMEs.

## Vendored/generated components retain their own licenses

- **`firmware-1-pluto-usb-ethernet/src/`** (not committed to this repo —
  fetched fresh by `setup.sh`) — a monolithic checkout combining Linux
  (GPL-2.0), U-Boot (GPL-2.0+), and Buildroot (mostly MIT/BSD, individual
  packages carry their own licenses) from
  https://github.com/Xiaozhang-code-cloud/Fish-Wan-plutosdr-fw-7020-SDR.
  This repo's `patches/*.patch` files are diffs against that GPL-licensed
  source and are intended to be applied to and distributed with it; treat
  them as inheriting the GPL-2.0 terms of the files they modify when
  combined with that source.

- **`tools/legacy-libs/`** — prebuilt compatibility shared libraries
  (`libtinfo`, `libncurses`, `libssl`, `libcrypto` and friends) sourced from
  Ubuntu's package archive, redistributed here only so Vivado 2022.2 can run
  on Linux distributions that no longer ship these versions. They retain
  their original upstream licenses (ncurses: MIT-style; OpenSSL: Apache
  License 2.0). See each distribution's own packaging for exact license
  text; these are unmodified upstream binaries.

- Xilinx Vivado/Vitis itself, and any AMD/Xilinx IP referenced by the HDL
  projects, are proprietary and licensed separately by AMD/Xilinx — not
  covered by this repository at all.
